# Nuxt conventions

- App routes are a SPA (`ssr: false`); marketing/legal pages are prerendered. Pages are thin: compose feature components and composables.
- **No business logic in the client.** Nuxt server routes are not an API; FastAPI owns every rule. Validation in the client is UX only and mirrors server schemas.
- Auth and workspace selection live in route middleware (`middleware/auth.ts`, `middleware/workspace.ts`); the active workspace id is sent as `X-Workspace-Id`.
- Server state: Vue Query via the generated Hey API client in `packages/api-client`. Pinia holds UI state only (panel open, density, filters not worth persisting server-side).
- Composables in `composables/` (`useJobs`, `useTrack`), auto-imported; one concern each; reactive params as `computed` so queries refetch.
- Forms: VeeValidate + Zod schemas generated from the OpenAPI spec; unsaved-changes guard on every editable form.
- i18n: user-facing strings go through `@nuxtjs/i18n` from day one.
- No React, no Next/TanStack Start idioms, no Nuxt UI default look; components come from `packages/ui`.
- Use `context7` for current Nuxt/Vue APIs before relying on memory.
